  "body": "Currently the spec says \"block scope\", but can we be more specific? For example: variable declarations are scoped to the closest ordered list or algorithm.\r\n\r\nThis would make this example from @tobie invalid:\r\n\r\n```\r\n1.  If condition, then let |result| be `\"foo\"`.\r\n1.  Otherwise, let |result| be `\"bar\"`.\r\n```\r\n\r\nBut I think it's better written as:\r\n\r\n```\r\n1. Let |result| be `\"foo\"` if condition, otherwise `\"bar\"`.\r\n```\r\n\r\nStep 3 of https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#http-network-fetch would also need tweaking.\r\n\r\nAlso, I think:\r\n\r\n> Variables must not be declared more than once per algorithm.\r\n\r\nWould be more clearly written as:\r\n\r\n> Variable names must be unique within an algorithm.\r\n\r\nI didn't realise the original statement was meant to prevent shadowing.",
